//! Observed acceptance transcript of the reference binary, replayed offline.
//!
//! GENERATED BY OBSERVATION, NOT BY HAND. Every row is the verdict `ffmpeg 8.1`
//! gave for one specifier or one `-map` value, recorded from the shipped
//! binary. D6 explicitly permits this: the reference is used as a black box
//! producing observed outputs, and no source was read.
//!
//! Reference: `ffmpeg version 8.1` (Homebrew, arm64 macOS, 2026),
//! `libavformat 62.12.100`.
//!
//! Regenerate with, for the specifier table:
//!
//! ```sh
//! ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc=size=64x48:rate=10:duration=1 \
//!        -f lavfi -i sine=frequency=440:duration=1 \
//!        -f lavfi -i sine=frequency=880:duration=1 \
//!        -map 0:v -map 1:a -map 2:a -c:v mpeg4 -c:a aac t.mkv
//! # then, for each candidate SPEC:
//! ffmpeg -nostdin -loglevel error -i t.mkv -c:"$SPEC" copy -f null -
//! ```
//!
//! and for the map table, `-map "$VALUE" -c copy` in place of `-c:"$SPEC"`.
//!
//! Two normalisations are applied to the captured stderr, both lossless for our
//! purposes:
//!
//! * The "Cannot combine multiple program/group designators…" line is emitted by
//!   the reference **without a trailing newline**, so the next log line is glued
//!   onto it. The glued suffix is stripped here; the missing newline is recorded
//!   as a D17 deviation in `crates/app/vaco-cli-core/src/error.rs`.
//! * A malformed `disp:` value makes the reference print two lines containing
//!   heap addresses before the stable "Invalid disposition specifier". Only the
//!   stable line is kept.
//!
//! The reference also prints `Parsed \'usable only\'` at error level **on the
//! success path** whenever a specifier contains `u`. It is filtered out here and
//! recorded as a D17 deviation; reproducing it is the binary\'s job, not this
//! crate\'s.

